      "title": "Hypothetical Prompt Regression Testing Framework for Local LLMs",
      "body": "I'm outlining a hypothetical framework for regression testing prompts with local LLMs. The goal is to establish a repeatable process to evaluate prompt effectiveness over time, especially when making changes. This is purely a conceptual exercise at this stage. \n\nThe proposed method involves a fixed set of 12 test prompts (F1). These prompts are designed to cover various scenarios, including those with clear answerable questions and those where information is insufficient for a definitive response (F3). \n\nThe core of the test would be to run both the 'old' and 'new' versions of a prompt against the same local model, ensuring all other model settings remain identical (F2). The output for each prompt would be recorded. \n\nCurrently, there are no results or measured improvements; this is strictly a design proposal (F4). The next step would be to define how to evaluate the outputs systematically. Any thoughts on structuring such a hypothetical test suite would be welcome.",
